      "theory_name": "Theories of Spatial Reference Frames in Haptic Perception",
      "commitment_type": "reviews",
      "specific_claim": "The paper reviews and synthesizes theories on how different spatial reference frames (e.g., egocentric, allocentric, hand-centered, object-centered) are utilized and transformed during haptic perception of object orientation."
    },
    {
      "theory_name": "Active Touch Theory",
      "commitment_type": "reviews",
      "specific_claim": "The paper reviews the concept that haptic perception of spatial orientation is an active process involving motor exploration and integration of sensory feedback, rather than passive reception of stimuli."
    }
  ],
